  "name": "ANTI PHOSPHOLIPID - IgM (APL IgM)",
  "code": "APL IgM",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"288\">\n<p data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"288\">Antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) are autoantibodies directed against phospholipid&ndash;protein complexes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"372\">\n<p data-start=\"291\" data-end=\"372\">The <strong data-start=\"295\" data-end=\"310\">IgM subtype</strong> is one of the three major types tested (<strong data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"368\">IgG, IgM, IgA</strong>).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"373\" data-end=\"544\">\n<p data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"454\">They are associated with <strong data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"435\">Antiphospholipid Syndrome (APS)</strong>, which leads to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"457\" data-end=\"544\">\n<li data-start=\"457\" data-end=\"490\">\n<p data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"490\">Arterial or venous thrombosis</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"521\">\n<p data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"521\">Recurrent pregnancy loss</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"521\">Thrombocytopenia</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
